/**
 * @defgroup dl_modules Deep Learning Modules and Layers
 * @brief Core tensor/graph infrastructure, layers, optimizers (SGD with momentum, Adam, AdamW,
 *        parameter groups, learning-rate schedules, gradient clipping), losses, checkpoints and
 *        safetensors I/O, seeding and deterministic mode, benchmarking, and device backends
 *        with their caching allocator -- the building blocks every other group is composed
 *        from.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup interpretability Interpretability
 * @brief Post-hoc explanation methods applied to an already-trained model: whole-model LRP
 *        over the rules built into each layer in @ref dl_modules, plus model-agnostic and
 *        gradient-based explainers, and metrics and baselines for judging an explanation's
 *        quality.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup interpretability_agnostic Model-Agnostic Explainers
 * @ingroup interpretability
 * @brief Tools that don't depend on a particular explainer: perturbation explainers that only
 *        need a model's input/output behavior, explanation-quality metrics (faithfulness,
 *        randomization, complexity), the null-model baseline, and dense matrix decompositions
 *        for analysing activations and weights.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup interpretability_dl Gradient-Based Explainers
 * @ingroup interpretability
 * @brief Explainers that use a model's gradients, activations, or internal structure
 *        directly.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup interpretability_lrp Layer-wise Relevance Propagation
 * @ingroup interpretability
 * @brief Whole-model LRP (LRP, LRPTarget, LRPSeed), rule selection (LRPRule, LRPRuleConfig),
 *        Zennit-style composites (lrp_composite), conservation checks, and BatchNormFold (folds
 *        an eval-mode BatchNorm into the preceding layer before LRP).
 */

/**
 * @defgroup rl Reinforcement Learning
 * @brief Environments, agents, and training algorithms (DQN, REINFORCE, A2C, PPO, SAC) built
 *        on the @ref dl_modules tensor/autograd core.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup mech_interp Mechanistic Interpretability
 * @brief Tools for inspecting and probing a model's internal computation directly --
 *        activation caching, linear probes, sparse autoencoders, circuit graphs -- plus the
 *        GFlowNet-based non-goal-directed training objectives motivated by the Scientist AI
 *        research direction.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup neuro_symbolic Neuro-Symbolic Reasoning
 * @brief A differentiable fuzzy-logic core (Logic Tensor Networks-shaped t-norm/t-conorm
 *        operators, a p-mean quantifier aggregator, and a satisfaction loss trainable via
 *        ordinary gradient descent) plus a from-scratch Datalog engine (bottom-up fixpoint
 *        evaluation, a real-valued/weighted generalization, and a hand-derived LRP rule) --
 *        and a bridge wiring a real neural predicate's output in as a Datalog base fact's
 *        weight, so relevance traces from a symbolic derivation back into the network.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup data_pipeline Data Loading, Transformation & Validation
 * @brief Dataset/IterableDataset/DataLoader/Transform/Compose/CollateFn core, plus concrete
 *        modality implementations (tabular CSV, image, text, audio, a reduced-scope video
 *        frame-directory stub) and generic dataset validation (descriptive statistics,
 *        missingness/outlier detection), all built on the @ref dl_modules Tensor.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup evolutionary Evolutionary Computation
 * @brief A from-scratch, DEAP-free genetic-algorithm core (population/fitness/selection/
 *        crossover/mutation, NSGA-II), plus neuroevolution (NEAT, Evolution Strategies),
 *        evolutionary hyperparameter optimization (CMA-ES), Population Based Training, and
 *        evolutionary generative-model training (E-GAN) built on top of it.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup visualization Visualization
 * @brief Visualization in two layers. Always built in the core library and unit-tested:
 *        versioned JSON documents (`json.hpp`, `viz/document.hpp`: `pulsatrix.<kind>.v1` for
 *        attributions, heatmaps, token relevance, circuit graphs, training logs and feature
 *        dashboards), dependency-free SVG figures (`viz/svg.hpp`, also the `pulsatrix_svg`
 *        tool), and the data transforms (`plot_data.hpp`/`colormap.hpp`). Opt-in via
 *        `PULSATRIX_ENABLE_VIZ`: live Dear ImGui + ImPlot widgets and dashboards that read the
 *        same data, checked through the demo apps under `examples/viz/` rather than GoogleTest,
 *        since a live window context isn't testable headlessly.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup hyperparameter_optimization Hyperparameter Optimization
 * @brief A typed SearchSpace/Configuration/Trial core plus grid/random search, Bayesian
 *        optimization (Gaussian-process and TPE surrogates), and bandit-based early stopping
 *        (Successive Halving, Hyperband, ASHA) -- also consumed directly by @ref evolutionary
 *        CMA-ES and Population Based Training.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup system_monitoring System Monitoring
 * @brief Live CPU/GPU utilization, memory and temperature sampling with a streaming JSON
 *        Lines / CSV log (SystemMonitor). Every metric a platform cannot read is reported as
 *        missing (std::nullopt) with a discoverable reason -- never as a fabricated zero.
 */
